{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/focusmode_foot

    The foot of the content in focus mode: the completion line and the previous and next row.

    The theme's core renderer prints it with core's activity navigation, under the activity's own
    content, on every page that can switch focus mode in place. The container is shown only under
    the focus mode body class: the ordinary skin has the activity information box, which states the
    same conditions (decision D3 keeps the discreet line and accepts the hidden duplicate).

    The conditions come through core's own partial, so the wording and the icons stay identical to
    the course page's. The list wraps it in a ul because core 5.3's activity_info does, and the
    partial emits an li there. The loop lives inside a section carrying istrackeduser, because the
    partial reads that flag from the enclosing context, exactly as activity_info arranges it.

    Context variables required for this template (described without braces, because a Mustache
    comment closes at the first pair of closing braces it meets):

    * completion - false, or an object with istrackeduser and completiondetails
    * activitynav - core's previous and next row, rendered, or the empty string
    * hasactivitynav - whether there is a row to draw

    Example context (json):
    {
        "completion": {
            "istrackeduser": true,
            "completiondetails": [
                {"statusincomplete": 1, "description": "View"}
            ]
        },
        "activitynav": "<div class=\"activity-navigation\">Next</div>",
        "hasactivitynav": true
    }
}}
<div class="dimensions-focus-only dimensions-focus-foot">
    {{#completion}}
        <div class="dimensions-focus-completion">
            <span class="dimensions-focus-completion-kicker">{{#str}}focusmode_completionkicker, theme_dimensions{{/str}}</span>
            <ul class="dimensions-focus-completion-list">
                {{#completiondetails}}
                    {{> core_course/completion_automatic }}
                {{/completiondetails}}
            </ul>
        </div>
    {{/completion}}
    {{#hasactivitynav}}
        <div class="dimensions-focus-activitynav">
            {{{activitynav}}}
        </div>
    {{/hasactivitynav}}
</div>
